{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:0684802524cfc2204abeabaebe46aa023dd15afef9d2f0dad195e84c63b42674","title":"What counts as one possible observation must be fixed before comparing cosmological likelihoods. Perceptions, scientific records, planets, and causal pasts are alternative choices of observational description, with different contents and possible overlap.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0002"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:06fc2e875179b953fd421e410fe6c2bd2645320182c64be3e44125cc7f1d823d","title":"Can local generators of global internal symmetries be constructed from local implementations of the flip on a doubled theory, and can conserved Wightman currents be recovered by shrinking the generators' localization regions to a point?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0006"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:06190326ea6557dddf43224caad297e2d6d26f18696ed51af1f77bea3720db49","title":"Which properties of the fake superpotential W extend from extremal horizons to the entire radial flow, and how can W and the ADM mass be determined for small black holes without finite-moduli attractor points?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0008"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:06125df0e581908a22666711b19be818bae7b108a8a6aa88d68acd759f0171b7","title":"Can Type IIB modulus stabilisation generate TeV-scale strings with two micron-sized dimensions and four much smaller dimensions, while determining the associated light spectrum and phenomenological constraints?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0010"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:06d0fff814a1ccfbc9c6fc6722b6a758f63b71fbbda46dffd5e1745f57d4723b","title":"Under what conditions can gauge-mediated supersymmetry breaking survive early-universe evolution: selection of a metastable SUSY-breaking vacuum, decay of the spurion, thermal stability of a volume modulus, and acceptable gravitino production?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0012"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0618df9ef5270ad464fe1f01dd08ec7efd7d2d4340dd4f9ce65b160fb9b0ab17","title":"Can rare interactions of energetic, nonthermal axionic dark radiation affect BBN, produce dark matter after thermal freeze-out, and leave an observable cosmic axion background?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0014"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:0647b23fdbab1b882f600a99ae63de7ff213a9a09472be29b7be95668740c6d3","title":"Can a collapsing object bounce from a black-hole-like trapped phase into an outgoing white-hole phase while satisfying Einstein's equations outside a finite quantum region, and can small exterior quantum effects accumulate long enough to permit this transition?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0016"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:064e45cac359c65b5666e5cdabea82f8e2ce81376982c45a5c8c063117e250ce","title":"Which rational-section configurations in codimension-two fibers permit which U(1) matter charges in F-theory, particularly for SU(5) fundamental, antisymmetric and singlet matter? Can the singlet configurations organize Higgsing to discrete gauge symmetries?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0019"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:06c88b880df8b96f5292d117c9f80fc770720e6ef57c9e8a5983aff82ec6df15","title":"How much supersymmetry survives an internal compactification? The relevant data are globally covariantly constant spinors and the action of internal holonomy on the parent spin representation.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0026"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:06ed440b64f24540a1d19e641adf84ff8e7c6520ec0e93574de0b298d63423be","title":"Massless scalars can affect black-hole extremality through gauge couplings and affect probe interactions through derivatives of the probe mass. The effective theory keeps these two mechanisms distinct before imposing a relation between them.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0034"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:060ca229597c675883b8795f21efbaeb7beb61bb72c17d107bd6390b31893f9b","title":"What constraints does the adopted fuzzball resolution of the black-hole information paradox place on cosmology, and could virtual compression-resistant fuzzballs explain a small effective cosmological constant?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0037"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:069b7aa0270ab7a02d19967e4eee07bf4dab53bab765a4543dffe859904d10e5","title":"How can positive late-time energy coexist with the exact-potential restriction? The paper considers a metastable perturbative vacuum and a rolling scalar configuration.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:064b7795efc4138b39aad15c1bf22b7af51cdffb4c9791597112dcf3dc6a5185","title":"Does repeatedly restoring fields and defects lead to the complete allowed background category, and does its cobordism vanish?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0045"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:06ff32af3507514e3e6c131e1e11dc63bc09bb60b6dd79f5f984967e422beaec","title":"The rigid quotient supplies an explicit setting for comparing Bianchi formulations and testing positive stationary potentials. Its retained sector has three Kähler moduli and no complex-structure moduli.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0045"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:06